fields.value:

{{Stealnotes
| name = Wukong's Command
| desc = Additionally grants {{A|Monkey King|Jingu Mastery}} despite not showing in any of the stolen ability slots.<br><br>Clones still provide {{M|vision}}, but they stop attacking and moving upon losing the ability. Soldiers from the previous cast neither continue attacking nor moving upon re-acquiring ability.
| is_behavenormal = yes
}}

 * {{Symbol|Target|Area}}
** Upon cast, all Clones immediately move to their predetermined spot within the formation in {{#var:Wukong's Command basic2}}-speed.
** The ability has three main components:
*** The {{Symbol|Wukong}} {{M|Clone|text=Clone Soldiers}}.
*** The command rings.
*** {{Symbol|bonus agh}} {{Symbol|a|Counter}} The passive Clone Soldier timer.

* [[File:Dota2 Condition-1.png|21px|1]] The {{Symbol|Wukong}} {{M|Clones}} have the following properties:
** {{M|Hidden}}
** {{M|Invulnerable}}
** {{M|Phase movement}}
** {{M|Unobstructed movement}}
** Uncontrollable
** {{M|Unselectable}}
** {{Symbol|Vision|Base}}
*** Has a 600 {{M|daytime}} and {{M|nighttime}} [[vision]] radius.
** Benefit from all {{M|attributes}} increasing sources and specifically {{Symbol|bonus agh}} {{A|Monkey King|Jingu Mastery}}-based {{M|talent|t=t2l}}, except the following:
*** Other {{M|talent|t=t0}} bonuses, as they do not utilize active abilities.
*** Permanent {{M|buffs}}, except {{Symbol|bonus agh}} {{Symbol|bonus shd}} ability upgrades.
*** Copies most items within the [[#Clone Inventory|clones' inventory]], the Clones may utilize the following mechanics:
**** {{M|Attack modifier}}.
**** {{M|Aura}}
*** The Clone's current attributes corresponds to the Wukong's, and adapts per ability cast.
** {{Symbol|Attack Damage}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
*** The Clones have a fixed {{#var:Wukong's Command value4}}-second attack interval, they only attack visible enemy heroes within their {{M|vision}} range, and within the command ring radius.
*** Considers enemy {{M|clones}}, {{M|illusions}}, and {{M|creep-heroes}} as heroes.
*** The attack interval has the following properties:
**** The interval counts down regardless if the attack is successful or {{M|misses}}.
**** Affected by {{M|attack animation}} sources, but not {{M|attack speed}} sources.

[[File:Dota2 Monkey King Wukong's Command Formation.jpg|thumb|250px|Wukong's Command Clones' formations.]]

* [[File:Dota2 Condition-2.png|21px|2]] [[File:Dota2 Monkey King Wukong Ring-1.png|84px|1st Ring Radius]][[File:Dota2 Monkey King Wukong Ring-2.png|84px|2nd Ring Radius]][[File:Dota2 Monkey King Wukong Ring-3.png|84px|3rd Ring Radius]]
** All command rings have the following properties:
*** The {{Symbol|Target|Area}} blue area indicates the Clones' {{M|attack range}}.
*** The first Soldier is always {{M|Facing Angle|text=facing|t=u}} North, [[Wikipedia:Perpendicular|perpendicular]] ({{Code|90°}}) to its corresponding command ring radius.
*** The Soldier's formation is always the same, except when the ability is cast at the map edges.
** {{Symbol|Wukong}}
*** The Clones dissipate in the following conditions:
**** Whenever Wukong moves away from the command radius.
**** Successive cast immediately end the current instance.
**** Upon Wukong's {{M|death}}.

* [[File:Dota2 Condition-3.png|21px|3]] {{Symbol|a|Counter}}
** The timer applies a hidden countdown on Wukong, and does nothing by default. 
** {{cf|aghnotes}} Hence, acquiring the {{M|Aghanim's Scepter|text=ability upgrade}} immediately spawns a Clone, since the passive Clone spawn component utilizes a fixed restore time.
*** {{Symbol|Charges}}
**** However, upon restoring a [[charge]], but Wukong's condition does not allow passive spawns, the Clone is spawned as soon as the conditions allow it to.
*** {{Symbol|Affect|Self}}
**** Does not spawn clones while Wukong is affected by the following sources:
***** {{A|Monkey King|Mischief}} {{M|Transformation Ability|text=transformed}}.
***** Either the {{A|Monkey King|Tree Dance}} {{Code|bounce_leap}} or {{Code|bounce_perch}} {{M|buffs}}.
***** {{M|Hidden}}
***** {{M|Invisible}}
***** Upon Wukong's {{M|death}}.
*** {{Symbol|bonus agh}} {{Symbol|Wukong}}
**** Does not attack {{M|Roshan}} and the {{M|Tormentor}}.

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Wukong's Command icon0}}
| desc = Monkey King creates a circular formation of soldiers that spread out from his position. If Monkey King leaves the area his soldiers disperse. The soldiers have Monkey King's attack that attacks at a fixed rate of 1.1s, and only targets enemy Heroes. Monkey King is granted bonus armor for the spell's duration.<br><br>Monkey King can transform into any one of his soldiers during Wukong's command, taking its place for a short duration, becoming indistinguishable from other soldiers, and leaving another soldier in his stead.
}}
* The command rings have the following additional properties:
** [[File:Dota2 Monkey King Wukong Ring-1.png|84px]] The 1<sup>st</sup> ring forms a [[Wikipedia:Pentagon|pentagon]] within {{#var:Wukong's Command value1}} radius, with the Soliders {{#expr:360/{{#var:Wukong's Command type1 value2}}}}° apart.
** [[File:Dota2 Monkey King Wukong Ring-2.png|84px]] The 2<sup>nd</sup> ring forms a [[Wikipedia:Nonagon|nonagon]] within {{#var:Wukong's Command value2}} radius, with the Soliders {{#expr:360/{{#var:Wukong's Command type1 value3}}}}° apart.
** [[File:Dota2 Monkey King Wukong Ring-3.png|84px]] The 3<sup>rd</sup> ring forms a [[Wikipedia:Heptagon|heptagon]] within {{Symbol|bonus t4l}} {{ValueColor||{{#var:Wukong's Command value3 tal}}|25tal}} radius, with the Soliders {{ValueColor||{{#expr:360/{{#var:Wukong's Command type1 value4 tal}} round2}}°|25tal}} apart.

* {{cf|aghnotes}} The passive Clone spawn {{M|building}} attack restriction is not applied to {{M|ranged}} heroes.

* {{cf|talnotes}} The {{ValueColor||additional command ring|25tal}} {{M|talent|t=t4l}} also increases the ability's {{M|cast range}}.

